# Video engine

This repo's **production videos** are the `channel/` documentary engine, not `graph/` `ideate`. A title naming a real person belongs on `python -m channel generate`, never the LangGraph topic flow.

Canonical command: `python -m channel generate --channel <mode> --title "<title>"`. Drop-folder cut: `python -m channel drop --channel <mode> --title "<title>"` then assemble. Jobs live in `artifacts/<JOB_ID>/`. Specs: `docs/video-engine/`. Operator loop is the **master prompt** (`channel/master_prompt.py` / `MASTER`): same stages on every channel, DNA customized per mode. Copy the grammar in `docs/video-engine/QUALITY_BAR.md`; never clone a reference-cut spine.

```text
DO NOT MODIFY THE VIDEO ENGINE, CHANNEL PROMPTS, GLOBAL STYLE, MODEL CONFIGURATION, OR QA THRESHOLDS DURING A NORMAL VIDEO GENERATION TASK.
```

Images: operator **Google Flow** stills from `flow_prompts.txt` only after `originality_score ≥ 80` and `ready_to_publish`, or drop-folder stills named `[00-00]_….jpg`. Voice: **imported audio** (`ingest-audio` or a file in `drop/`). Engine never calls ElevenLabs or Flow. Shipped recuts may still use Kokoro (`am_liam` / roster). No silent provider fallback. Drop-folder cuts assemble without burned captions.

After a production change, update `docs/custom-videos.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `.cursor/rules/custom-videos.mdc` together. `tests/test_channel_handoff.py` guards the surfaces.
